X_umap = score_filtered(:,1:50);

Y_umap = umap(X_umap);

figure; %[output:6681030f]

gscatter( ... %[output:6681030f]
    Y_umap(:,1), ... %[output:6681030f]
    Y_umap(:,2), ... %[output:6681030f]
    dfsEvent); %[output:6681030f]

xlabel("UMAP 1"); %[output:6681030f]
ylabel("UMAP 2"); %[output:6681030f]
title("UMAP of gene expression by DFS event status"); %[output:6681030f]

legend( ... %[output:6681030f]
    "Censored", ... %[output:6681030f]
    "Recurred/Progressed", ... %[output:6681030f]
    "Location","best"); %[output:6681030f]

grid on; %[output:6681030f]

saveas(gcf, "figures/UMAP_geneexpression_DFS_reduced.png"); %[output:6681030f]
%[text] Before UMAP, the expression data were reduced to the first 50 principal components. This was done to remove very low-variance dimensions and reduce computational burden while retaining the major structure of the gene-expression data. Fifty PCs were used as a practical compromise: enough components to preserve substantial biological variation, while avoiding direct UMAP fitting on thousands of genes.
%[text] UMAP visualization of the filtered gene-expression data also showed substantial overlap between censored and recurred/progressed patients, with no clear cluster separation by DFS event status. This suggests that the overall expression structure is not strongly driven by DFS group membership.
%[text] 
