%[text] UMAP colored by tumor stage showed substantial overlap between Stage II, III and IV tumors, with no clear stage-specific clustering in the gene-expression space. This suggests that tumor stage is not the main driver of the global expression structure in this cohort.
%%
%[text] 11\. Heatmap with hierarchical clustering 
%[text] 50 most variable genes
filteredGeneVariance = var(expression_dfs_filtered, 0, 2);

[~, idxTop] = maxk(filteredGeneVariance, 50);

topExpression = expression_dfs_filtered(idxTop, :);

% Standardize each gene across patient
topExpressionZ = zscore(topExpression, 0, 2);

figure; %[output:25627d83]

imagesc(topExpressionZ); %[output:25627d83]

xlabel("Patients"); %[output:25627d83]
ylabel("Top 50 variable genes"); %[output:25627d83]
title("Top 50 most variable genes"); %[output:25627d83]

colorbar; %[output:25627d83]
saveas(gcf, "figures/heatmap_50variablegenes.png"); %[output:25627d83]
%[text] Very noisy heatmap, so next step is cluster the patients and the 50 genes:
% Cluster patients
patientDistance = pdist(topExpressionZ', 'euclidean');
patientTree = linkage(patientDistance, 'average');
patientOrder = optimalleaforder(patientTree, patientDistance);

% Cluster genes
geneDistance = pdist(topExpressionZ, 'euclidean');
geneTree = linkage(geneDistance, 'average');
geneOrder = optimalleaforder(geneTree, geneDistance);

% Reorder matrix
topExpressionZ_clustered = ...
    topExpressionZ(geneOrder, patientOrder);

figure; %[output:5f147f48]

imagesc(topExpressionZ_clustered); %[output:5f147f48]

xlabel("Patients"); %[output:5f147f48]
ylabel("Top 50 variable genes"); %[output:5f147f48]
title("Clustered heatmap of top 50 most variable genes"); %[output:5f147f48]

colorbar; %[output:5f147f48]
saveas(gcf, "figures/clusteredheatmap_50variablegenes.png"); %[output:5f147f48]
%[text] Add DFS annotation:
% Reorder DFS status using clustered patient order
dfsClustered = dfsEvent(patientOrder);

% Main heatmap
figure; %[output:95df27ae]

ax1 = axes('Position',[0.1 0.15 0.75 0.68]); %[output:95df27ae]

imagesc(ax1, topExpressionZ_clustered); %[output:95df27ae]

xlabel(ax1, "Patients"); %[output:95df27ae]
ylabel(ax1, "Top 50 variable genes"); %[output:95df27ae]

colorbar(ax1); %[output:95df27ae]

% DFS annotation strip
ax2 = axes('Position',[0.1 0.85 0.75 0.04]); %[output:95df27ae]

imagesc(ax2, dfsClustered'); %[output:95df27ae]

yticks(ax2, []); %[output:95df27ae]
xticks(ax2, []); %[output:95df27ae]

title(ax2, "DFS status"); %[output:95df27ae]

colormap(ax2, [0 0.4470 0.7410; 0.8500 0.3250 0.0980]); %[output:95df27ae]
saveas(gcf, "figures/clusteredheatmap_50variablegenes_DFS.png"); %[output:95df27ae]
%[text] Hierarchical clustering of the 50 most variable genes did not reveal clear patient groups corresponding to DFS status. Censored and recurrent/progressed patients were interspersed across the expression-based clusters, consistent with the PCA and UMAP results showing no strong global separation by DFS outcome.

